PVD("samoa_vision_2021-2040",{"docs":["","688ff795095ccc71f0261315_Samoa 2040"],"s":{"1":[[1,"8","1","Labour Mobility for Domestic Productivity","Given the small size of the local market, labour mobility can be a means of improving the productivity of the domestic labour force by providing it with access to opportunities in overseas markets.",""],[1,"10","6","Labour Mobility Promotion and Worker Support Measures","To achieve these objectives, sustained efforts will be required to connect and market Samoan workers to overseas employers.",""],[1,"10","6","Regular Review of Recruitment and Selection Processes","Recruitment and selection processes should be regularly reviewed to ensure that employer needs are being met.",""],[1,"10","6","Alignment of Education and Training with Labour Market Demand","Domestic education and training should be aligned as closely as possible with labour market demand from both domestic and overseas employers.",""],[1,"10","6","Expansion of Labour Mobility and Preferential Migration Opportunities","The government should also continue to advocate for the expansion of labour mobility and preferential migration opportunities available to Samoa.",""],[1,"10","6","Support for Samoan Workers Before and During Overseas Employment","Government must closely support Samoan workers at all stages of the process - prior to departure, to ensure they are adequately prepared; while they are overseas, to manage feelings of isolation and",""],[1,"54","1","Labour Mobility Promotion and Worker Placement Support","To achieve these objectives, sustained efforts will be required to connect and market Samoan workers to overseas employers.",""],[1,"54","1","Recruitment and Selection Process Review","Recruitment and selection processes should be regularly reviewed to ensure that employer needs are being met.",""],[1,"54","1","Alignment of Education and Training with Labour Market Demand","Domestic education and training should be aligned as closely as possible with labour market demand from both domestic and overseas employers.",""],[1,"54","1","Advocacy for Expanded Labour Mobility and Preferential Migration","The government should also continue to advocate for the expansion of labour mobility and preferential migration opportunities available to Samoa.",""],[1,"54","2","Migrant Worker Support and Reintegration Measures","government must closely support Samoan workers at all stages of the process - prior to departure, to ensure they are adequately prepared; while they are overseas, to manage feelings of isolation and ensure they are in the best possible position to meet employer expectations; and upon their return to Samoa to help facilitate their reintegration.",""],[1,"56","10","Seasonal Employment Expansion Initiative","I have tasked the implementing government agencies to explore every opportunity available to ensure that we capitalize on the opportunity to secure more jobs for Samoans.",""],[1,"56","11","Zero Tolerance Blacklist for Deported Workers","Samoa has adopted the zero tolerance policy which blacklist any workers deported for violating conditions of their employment contracts.",""],[1,"57","1","Pacific Labour Scheme Recruitment and Worker Transition","SWP employers are also now recruiting under the Pacific Labour Scheme (PLS) and moving SWP workers across to the PLS on longer- term contracts.",""],[1,"57","4","Overseas Labour Mobility Promotion and Support","Doing so will require active government efforts to connect and market Samoan workers to overseas employers, and to help ensure that the good reputation of Samoan workers is maintained.",""],[1,"57","4","Overseas Employer and Worker Outreach Support","Government should hone its ability to reach out to employers and workers overseas in order to provide support, resolve issues, and ensure that employer expectations and requirements are being met.",""],[1,"57","4","Coordinated and Adequately Resourced Labour Mobility Arrangements","Ensuring that these arrangements are well- coordinated and adequately resourced should be a priority.","The Ministry of Commerce, Industry and Labour"],[1,"57","6","Labour Market-Aligned TVET and PSET Training","TVET and Post-School Education Training (PSET) program providers in Samoa should target the fields in demand under the schemes, with support and resources from government and development partners (including APTC).",""],[1,"57","6","English and Interview Skills Support","Additional resourcing in key areas, including English language skills and interview skills, could be considered.",""],[1,"57","6","Labour Market Information Collection and Dissemination System","This will involve continued efforts to collect and disseminate data from several sources, such as employer surveys, job advertisements, and the issuance of work permits for foreign workers in Samoa.",""],[1,"57","6","Labour Market Information Analysis for Training Planning","The regular analysis and use of labour market information to inform training can also help to address employer concerns about skills shortages.",""],[1,"57","7","Broader Labour Mobility Pathways Strategy","Samoa should also look to opportunities beyond the SWP and PLS in Australia, and the RSE, AIP and Pacific Trades Partnership in NZ, as part of its broader approach to labour mobility.",""],[1,"58","1","Advocacy for Expanded Labour Mobility and Preferential Migration Opportunities","The Government of Samoa should also continue to advocate for the expansion of labour mobility and preferential migration opportunities overseas.",""],[1,"58","2","Government Advocacy for Samoa's Labour Market Access in Australia","In Australia, there is also a role for advocacy and government- to-government dialogue to ensure that schemes such as the PLS and SWP remain in place and that changes to other work visa arrangements (such as the Working Holiday Maker (WHM) visa) do not adversely affect opportunities for Samoans.",""],[1,"58","2","Advocacy for Improved Access to Australian Labour Market Visas","The government could also advocate for improved access to Australia's labour market via other visa categories, including preferential visas such as the Working Holiday Maker visa which currently exclude Samoa.",""],[1,"58","5","Liaison Officer and Pastoral Care Support for Seasonal Workers","The appointment of Liaison Officers to manage workers in NZ and Australia as well as the provision of pastoral care helps to mitigate these risks.",""],[1,"58","5","Pre-departure Preparation and Training for Seasonal Workers","Preparing seasonal workers as part of pre-departure programs and trainings is also critical.",""],[1,"58","7","Community-Based Support Programs for Workers' Families","Community-based and led support programs for these families need to be strengthened.",""],[1,"58","7","Referral Services for Domestic Violence and Income Support","Adequate referral services (around domestic violence and income support, when workers fail to remit) must be made available",""],[1,"58","7","Resource Allocation for Accessible Support Services","the government may have to allocate resources to ensure these services are accessible.",""],[1,"58","8","Tailored Overseas Labour Mobility Selection Processes","To manage these risks, selection processes for overseas schemes can be tailored to ensure that appropriate incentives are in place - for example, by targeting those who are informally employed in the Samoan agriculture sector for agricultural seasonal work opportunities overseas.",""],[1,"58","8","Returnee Savings Guidance and Productive Investment Support","Returnees should also be provided with the guidance necessary to ensure that their savings are invested prudently and productively.",""],[1,"58","11","Remittance Fee Reduction Initiatives","The reduction of remittance fees is another objective worth pursuing.",""],[1,"63","7","Labour Mobility Upskilling Programme","To promote labour mobility, upskilling workers in the areas most in demand by host country employers is critical.",""]],"2":[[1,"32","2","Tourism Market Expansion and Product Development","More can be done to tailor marketing and product development (restaurants, shopping, activities, etc) to attract Chinese tourists, and identify specific segments of the Chinese market that match what Samoa has to offer.",""],[1,"32","3","Accommodation Pricing Coordination for Tourism Competitiveness","There needs to be a concerted effort by STA and the industry to price accommodation appropriately to entice tourists to choose Samoa over other destinations.",""],[1,"32","4","Tailored VFR Tourism Strategy","A tailored strategy for VFRs could usefully set out measures to increase the average spend per arrival (e.g. through incentives to stay in hotels and enjoy tourist services) and maximize the potential of this market, including as a source of support to the sector during the low season.",""],[1,"32","5","Visitor Segment Demand Analysis","While a detailed demand analysis will be required to evaluate and prioritize other visitor segments (including adventure, weddings, etc)",""],[1,"32","5","International Events Promotion Strategy","there has been some recent success in the hosting of international conferences, film, entertainment and sporting events which could be built on in the years ahead",""],[1,"32","5","Celebrity and Sports Icon Marketing Initiative","More can also be done to draw on the talents of celebrities and popular sports icons of Samoan descent to market Samoa",""]],"3":[[1,"9","5","Support for Agricultural Commercialization and Productivity Upgrade","Farmers will need to be supported in their efforts to transition from subsistence agriculture to semi-commercial and commercial production, including through the promotion of larger-scale farming, cooperative arrangements and producer organizations; the advancement of new climate-smart technologies and farming techniques, including via the provision of extension services; increased access to finance; and expanded provision of public infrastructure.",""],[1,"35","2","Support for Agricultural Commercialization and Productivity Upgrade","Farmers will need to be supported in their efforts to transition from subsistence agriculture to semi-commercial and commercial production, including through the promotion of larger-scale farming, cooperative arrangements and producer organizations; the advancement of new climate- smart technologies and farming techniques, including via the provision of extension services; increased access to finance; and expanded provision of public infrastructure.",""],[1,"39","4","Farmer Transition to Commercial Agriculture Support","In part, this will involve supporting farmers in their efforts to transition from subsistence agriculture to farming as a business, including through the promotion of larger-scale commercial farming and cooperative arrangements, the promotion of new technologies and farming techniques, and increasing access to finance and public infrastructure.",""],[1,"39","4","Agricultural Commercial Farming and Cooperative Promotion","In part, this will involve supporting farmers in their efforts to transition from subsistence agriculture to farming as a business, including through the promotion of larger-scale commercial farming and cooperative arrangements, the promotion of new technologies and farming techniques, and increasing access to finance and public infrastructure.",""],[1,"39","4","Agricultural Finance and Public Infrastructure Access Expansion","In part, this will involve supporting farmers in their efforts to transition from subsistence agriculture to farming as a business, including through the promotion of larger-scale commercial farming and cooperative arrangements, the promotion of new technologies and farming techniques, and increasing access to finance and public infrastructure.",""],[1,"41","1","Tailored Agricultural Finance and Matching Grant Support","Financial instruments should be provided that adapt to farmers' needs, with the cost of the financial subsidy implicit in such schemes transparently accounted for and financed by government or development partners.",""],[1,"41","1","Farmer Business Planning Support","Farmers should be supported in developing simple business plans which identify key inputs required and the potential revenues from their operations, based on market demand.",""],[1,"41","2","Agricultural Market Access and Storage Infrastructure Support","Access to public infrastructure is also required to help farmers connect with markets and ensure they can take advantage of production and storage facilities.",""],[1,"41","2","Rural Agricultural Infrastructure Development","Examples include field nurseries, rainwater harvesting structures, crop drying facilities, packhouses, slaughter and feed producing facilities, and cold storage facilities for fish.",""],[1,"41","2","Agricultural Access Road Rehabilitation and Extension","Government support for the rehabilitation and extension of access roads for targeted farmers with a proven record of consistent agricultural farming production should also be considered",""],[1,"41","2","Project Evaluation and Prioritization for Agricultural Infrastructure","The economic case for the public provision of such infrastructure should be assessed with project evaluation criteria, with prioritization based on the most critical bottlenecks facing the sector.",""]],"4":[[1,"8","1","ICT Connectivity for Overseas Value Chain Participation","Improved connectivity provided through new information and communication technologies (ICT) may provide new opportunities for Samoans to participate in overseas value chains and provide services for external markets, without having to leave the country.",""],[1,"10","2","Digital Connectivity Expansion","Further efforts are now required to get Samoans connected, and to strengthen the legal and regulatory environment to ensure that consumer interests are protected.",""],[1,"46","1","Digital Connectivity Expansion","further efforts are required to get Samoans connected",""],[1,"47","3","ICT Infrastructure Expansion and Cable Connectivity","These efforts to establish a robust ICT infrastructure help to meet a critical precondition for the development of a digital economy.",""],[1,"47","3","Manatua Cable Connection","Connecting to the Manatua cable will provide extra capacity and redundancy and this is also a step in the right direction.",""],[1,"47","3","Telecommunications Cost Reduction and Connectivity Expansion","More needs to be done to bring down costs and get Samoans connected.",""],[1,"47","3","Next-Generation Mobile Network Investment","A competitive telecommunications sector is crucial to ensure competitive prices for consumers and to stimulate investments in new technologies such as 4G+ and 5G.",""],[1,"51","2","ICT Infrastructure Expansion and Access Initiative","Ensure the necessary ICT infrastructure is in place, and that it is widely accessible;",""],[1,"65","5","ICT Infrastructure Investment","Further investments will be made in ICT, with the Manatua cable offering additional capacity and the potential to further reduce internet costs.",""]],"5":[[1,"49","5","Government Digital Services Expansion","With the recent expansion of broadband capacity comes the potential to digitize government processes and services including customs, business registry, and the payment of taxes and fees.",""],[1,"49","5","E-Health System Development","The development of an E-health system will improve the availability and management of patient health data and potentially allow a range of consultation services to be offered online.",""],[1,"49","5","E-Learning Platform Expansion","E-learning platforms could expand the range of educational content available to Samoan students and professionals and help alleviate capacity constraints.",""],[1,"50","1","National Digital ID System","As an important component of this agenda, a National Digital ID has the potential to expand access to goods and services (financial services in particular); to reduce fraud, protect rights, and increase transparency; and to promote efficiencies in the interaction between citizens and Government.",""],[1,"51","5","Government Digital Service Delivery and Process Digitization","government also needs to lead by example in providing e-health and education services, and in digitizing processes to reduce transactions costs and improve the efficiency of the government's interactions with the private sector.",""]],"6":[[1,"5","7","Strategy for the Development of Samoa Implementation and M&E Framework","The SDS will continue to lay out the strategy for Samoa's overall development, covering all the key pillars ranging from economic and social to environment considerations.",""],[1,"5","7","Samoa 2040 Monitoring through SDS M&E Process","The progress on the implementation of Samoa 2040 will be tracked through the SDS monitoring and evaluation process.",""],[1,"5","9","Samoa 2040 Implementation","I call on everyone to play his/her role in driving the successful implementation of the Samoa 2040 objectives and delivering a better quality of life for every Samoan.",""],[1,"12","7","Incorporation of Samoa 2040 Actions into the Development Strategy","Key actions derived from Samoa 2040 will be included in the SDS 2021-25, and future SDSs, these will monitor the implementation of these actions and the extent of progress against desired results.",""],[1,"14","2","Samoa 2040 Long-Term Strategic Vision and Action Monitoring Framework","It is therefore envisaged that four successive five-year SDSs - beginning with the 2021-25 SDS currently under preparation - will each reference Samoa 2040 as providing the long-term economic vision for the country.",""]],"7":[[1,"7","1","Samoa 2040 Economic Growth and Development Roadmap","Samoa 2040 sets Samoa's agenda for economic growth and development over the next 20 years.",""],[1,"8","1","Targeted Economic Opportunity Reforms and Investments","Reforms and investments should be targeted toward economic opportunities that have the most potential given Samoa's geography and unique circumstances.",""],[1,"8","1","Resilience-Building Investments for External Shocks","At the same time, investments need to focus on building resilience to external shocks, including natural disasters, public health emergencies, and the effects of climate change.",""],[1,"13","5","Targeted Reform and Investment Roadmap for Economic Growth","Samoa 2040 takes a realistic view of the constraints that geography imposes, but outlines what would be possible if existing opportunities for economic growth were fully exploited, and provides a roadmap of actions to unlock these opportunities.",""],[1,"13","6","Human Capital, Climate-Resilient Infrastructure, and Safe Environment Investment Package","Concerted efforts will be needed to improve the health, education, and training of Samoa's people, encourage investment in climate-resilient physical infrastructure to improve connectivity and lower costs, and provide a safe, secure environment for communities and businesses.",""],[1,"25","4","Human Capital Investment Promotion","Samoa will need to make concerted efforts to encourage investment in the health, education, and training of its people;",""],[1,"25","4","Climate-Resilient Infrastructure Investment","encourage investment in climate-resilient physical infrastructure to improve connectivity and lower costs;",""],[1,"25","4","Private Sector Investment Climate Support","ensure that government policy is supportive of long-term growth; and provide an attractive, stable economic environment to encourage private sector investment.",""]],"8":[[1,"9","2","Tourism Sector Repositioning and Coordination","Government must work together with the private sector to reposition tourism as a top national priority.",""],[1,"28","1","Tourism Sector Repositioning and Investment Support","Government must work together with the private sector to reposition tourism as a top national priority.",""],[1,"30","5","Whole-of-Government Tourism Development Strategy","to recommit to building tourism and reposition it as a national priority.",""],[1,"30","6","National Tourism Coordination Taskforce","A single high-level taskforce representing the key stakeholders across government, the private sector, and the community should be made accountable for driving the achievement of the Samoa 2040 tourism vision.",""],[1,"30","6","Tourism Sector Coordinating Authority","The establishment of a single coordinating authority to guide and be accountable for tourism sector development would help to overcome coordination failures and would be responsible for the detailed plans necessary to translate this vision into action.",""],[1,"30","6","Tourism Demand Analysis and Market Prioritization","Its initial priorities would include: i) the production of a detailed demand analysis that will evaluate and prioritize target markets;",""],[1,"30","6","Tourism Public Resource Allocation Analysis","ii) the completion of an economic analysis that will guide the allocation of public resources in support of tourism;",""],[1,"30","6","Tourism Destination Masterplan","iii) a comprehensive destination masterplan that links government expenditures to tourism outcomes and steers the public and private investments needed.",""],[1,"30","6","Samoa Tourism Authority Capacity Strengthening","Strengthening the skills and capacity of the Samoa Tourism Authority (STA) will be critical to supporting the work of the taskforce.",""],[1,"30","7","Public-Private Tourism Development Partnership","Government and the private sector must work together in driving tourism development forward, moving from a marketing-focused to an investment- oriented planning approach.",""],[1,"30","7","Tourism Policy Dialogue and Implementation Coordination","Key industry players and government representatives must engage together in the policy level discussions as well as during the implementation stage.",""]],"9":[[1,"8","5","Tourism Recovery Preparedness Measures","steps can be taken now to respond to this challenge.",""],[1,"30","2","Targeted Financial Support for Businesses","While borders remain closed, close coordination between the government and the private sector will be vital, as will the targeted provision of financial support.",""],[1,"30","2","Government-Private Sector Coordination for Border Closure Management","While borders remain closed, close coordination between the government and the private sector will be vital",""],[1,"30","2","COVID-19 Border Containment and Case Management Measures","Samoa's ability to contain the COVID-19 at the borders - while at the same time demonstrating its capacity to test for the virus, and to trace and treat / isolate any confirmed cases - will be vital",""]],"10":[[1,"9","2","Targeted Tourism Skills Development","A more coordinated, longer-term approach is required to promote skills development in targeted areas, enhance air access, and allocate public funding to projects and initiatives that will boost the attractiveness of Samoa as a tourist destination and unlock much-needed private investment in the local offering.",""],[1,"9","2","Air Access Enhancement for Tourism","A more coordinated, longer-term approach is required to promote skills development in targeted areas, enhance air access, and allocate public funding to projects and initiatives that will boost the attractiveness of Samoa as a tourist destination and unlock much-needed private investment in the local offering.",""],[1,"11","4","Hospitality Training Improvement Initiative","For tourism, boosting hospitality training to boost service standards is a priority.",""],[1,"28","1","Targeted Tourism Skills Development","A more coordinated, longer-term approach is required to promote skills development in targeted areas, enhance air access, and allocate public funding to initiatives that will unlock much-needed private investment in the local tourist offering.",""],[1,"28","1","Air Access Enhancement for Tourism","A more coordinated, longer-term approach is required to promote skills development in targeted areas, enhance air access, and allocate public funding to initiatives that will unlock much-needed private investment in the local tourist offering.",""],[1,"30","8","Air Access, Skills, Service Standards, and Public Infrastructure Support Measures","The demand analysis and masterplan will determine the specific government interventions required to facilitate air access, promote skills and service standards, and provide key public infrastructure and services.",""],[1,"31","1","Strategic Air Services Improvement Approach","Samoa needs to take a strategic and commercial approach to improving the capacity, frequency and reliability of services on key routes.",""],[1,"31","1","Aviation Sector Monitoring and Evaluation","Continued monitoring and evaluation of the Government's role in the aviation space is required to ensure that ongoing public ownership or subsidization has a clear economic rationale.",""],[1,"31","2","Hospitality Service Standards Improvement","Service standards in hotels and restaurants will require a substantial boost if the Samoa 2040 targets are to be achieved.",""],[1,"31","2","Post-Secondary and TVET Skills Development Upgrade","A longer-term approach to skills development is required, including improvements to the quality of training provided through post-secondary and Technical and Vocational Education and Training (TVET) programs, and a willingness to bring in expertise and skills from overseas as required.",""],[1,"31","2","Industry-Training Provider Collaboration Mechanism","Training providers should collaborate with industry to ensure that graduates are equipped with the requisite skills.",""],[1,"31","2","Hospitality Certificate Entry Requirement","Requiring a hospitality certificate as an entry point for employment in the tourist industry could help to ensure minimum service levels.",""],[1,"31","3","Strategic Public Investment in Tourism Enabling Infrastructure","Strategic public investments to develop key attractions and improve key public services and amenities will also assist in \"crowding in\" the private investment necessary to attract tourists from target markets.",""],[1,"32","1","Public Investment Support for Tourism Anchor Investments","In addition to providing complementary public investments - in connectivity, skills, and public services - in select cases the government may consider directly incentivize such private investments.",""],[1,"63","3","Hospitality Training for Tourism Service Standards","For tourism, boosting hospitality training to boost service standards is a priority, including through post- secondary and TVET programs, as well as international exposure.",""]],"11":[[1,"32","6","Tourism-Sector Local Agricultural Supply Linkages","Measures to improve the quantity, quality, and consistency of local agricultural supply to meet the demand from hotels and restaurants would lead to a higher proportion of tourist consumption being sourced locally.",""],[1,"32","6","Hotel-Farmer Supply Contract Scheme","Establishing supply contracts between hotels and established farmers could help to ensure a consistent supply of fruits and vegetables to tourism operators, and guaranteed income for the farmers.",""],[1,"50","3","Digital Tourism Platform Development","In tourism, digital booking and marketing platforms offer opportunities to increase access to international markets and broaden participation in the tourism sector, for example in accommodation (e.g. through Airbnb), tours, and transport.",""],[1,"50","3","Digital Connectivity and E-Commerce Enablement for Tourism","Improved access to reliable high-speed wifi, electronic payment systems, and e-content on attractions, history and culture will also help boost the attractiveness of Samoa as a tourist destination.",""]],"12":[[1,"11","4","Agricultural Extension and Farmer Support Services","In agriculture, farmers need technical information, support, and data on good agricultural practices, organic farming, pest control, livestock diseases, use of pesticides and compliance with export markets.",""],[1,"40","6","Agricultural Extension Service Expansion","the delivery of such services should be increased in line with the identified needs, either through expanding the capacity of the Ministry of Agriculture & Fishieries (MAF) to provide these services, or by utilizing the partnerships established between private sector and producers' groups to incentivize private delivery.","Ministry of Agriculture & Fishieries (MAF)"],[1,"40","6","Good Agricultural Practices and Integrated Pest Management Promotion","Good Agriculture Practices (GAP) and Integrated Pest Management (IPM) should be promoted by MAF though its extension and outreach system to discourage the use of herbicide and pesticides.","MAF"],[1,"40","6","Organic Farming Expansion and Regulation","The Government will be collaborating with certified organic groups to grow more coconut trees nationwide and regulate organic farming including the elimination of dual registration of certified farmers/farms.",""],[1,"40","6","Agricultural Inputs Market Oversight","Government has an important role in providing regulatory oversight of inputs and input markets including seeds, machinery, agrochemicals and fertilizers.",""],[1,"40","6","Technical Collaboration with Development Partners","Technical collaboration with development partners should be encouraged.",""],[1,"63","4","Agricultural and Fisheries Extension Support and Training","farmers and fishers need technical information, support, and data on good agricultural and fishing practices, organic farming, pest control, livestock diseases, use of pesticides and compliance with export markets.",""],[1,"63","4","Extension Service Provider Capacity Building","Providers of extension services need the training and skills necessary to be able to effectively respond to the needs of farmers.",""]],"13":[[1,"9","5","Strengthening Domestic and Export Market Linkages","Linkages with domestic and export markets should be strengthened in order to bolster demand.",""],[1,"9","5","Sustainable Fisheries Value Addition and Transshipment Support","In the fishing sector, there are opportunities to boost import substitution, increase the value of exports, and provide transshipment services, but the overexploitation of fishing resources must be avoided to preserve longer-term sustainability.",""],[1,"36","1","Strengthen Market Linkages for Demand Expansion","Linkages with domestic and export markets should be strengthened in order to bolster demand.",""],[1,"39","4","Agriculture and Fisheries Market Linkage Strengthening","For both agriculture and fishing, there is also the potential to strengthen linkages with domestic and export markets to bolster demand.",""],[1,"42","3","Agricultural Market Development and Value Chain Linkage Support","On the demand side, concerted efforts must be dedicated to developing both domestic and export markets.",""],[1,"42","4","Formal Supply Contract System for Agricultural Produce","establishment of formal supply contracts between farmers (or farmer cooperatives); manufacturers; and hotels and restaurants may help to ensure a reliable supply of fresh agricultural produce.",""],[1,"42","5","Trade Compliance and Export Market Expansion for Agricultural and Fish Products","Efforts should continue to improve compliance with the trade and quarantine arrangements and food safety standards that allow exports of agricultural produce to Australia, New Zealand, and other overseas markets.",""],[1,"42","5","Promotion of Samoan Products to Overseas Diaspora Markets","Efforts should also continue to promote Samoan- made products to the Samoan communities in Australia, New Zealand and the Unitied States.",""],[1,"42","5","Customs Regulations Amendment for Agriculture and Fisheries Investment","The opening up of the Customs (Development Projects) Regulations 2010 to include agriculture and fisheries development projects as qualifying projects is expected to boost agriculture and fisheries investments and therefore increase commercial agriculture and fisheries production.",""],[1,"42","5","Fisheries Competent Authority Establishment","The establishment of a Fisheries Competent Authority (FCA) - which would certify fish exports and ensure compliance with export market requirements - would allow fish to be exported to the European Union (EU) market and China, and may increase the price commanded by Samoa's fish exports.",""]],"14":[[1,"36","3","Agricultural Infrastructure and Practices Improvement","Improvements in farming infrastructure and practices will ultimately protect livelihoods across Samoa's population and help to ensure food security in the face of natural disasters and a changing climate.",""],[1,"40","3","Climate-Smart Agriculture Innovation Package","Innovations that promote climate-smart agriculture include climate change mitigation (intensification of livestock production, pasture management, improved feeding rations and practices using local products); and adaptation (by promoting tunnel houses to protect crops against heavy rains, water collection and small-scale irrigation to cope with prolonged dry seasons, resilient multi-tiered tree crop canopies and introduction of new higher-yield and drought-resistant crop varieties).",""],[1,"40","3","Climate-Resilience Research and Field Trials","Climate- resilience research should continue, including field trials to improve livestock and crop production and improve the availability and variety of nutritious food products.",""],[1,"40","3","Digital Farm Management and Climate Disaster Response Tools","Technologies such as Skyeye can be used to better manage farms and can also be an effective tool in designing responses to climate related disasters.",""]],"15":[[1,"39","4","National Fisheries Strategy Development","For fisheries in particular, an overall strategy needs to be put in place and the opportunity to provide transshipment services should be investigated further.",""],[1,"39","4","Fisheries Transshipment Services Feasibility Study","For fisheries in particular, an overall strategy needs to be put in place and the opportunity to provide transshipment services should be investigated further.",""],[1,"41","3","Community-Based Fisheries Management Plans","Community-Based Fisheries Management Plans (CBFMP) should be used to strengthen the management of coastal fisheries.",""],[1,"41","3","National Fisheries Strategic Plan","An overall strategic plan is required to define the key opportunities and set out the approach to achieving food security, boosting import substitution, and promoting exports.",""],[1,"41","3","Regional Fisheries Policy Dialogue with WCPFC","At the regional level, Samoa should engage in the dialogue with the Western and Central Pacific Fisheries Management Commission (WCPFC),",""],[1,"42","1","Support for Sustainable Management of Shared Oceanic Fisheries","Forum Fisheries Agency (FFA) and the Pacific Community (SPC) to help ensure the sustainable management of shared oceanic fisheries.",""]],"16":[[1,"10","2","Digital Skills and Literacy Investment","Investment in education and skills is vital to allow business owners and employees to make full use of digital technologies and innovate in ways that maximize its potential, while at the same time promoting the digital literacy of consumers.",""],[1,"11","4","Digital Skills and Awareness Development","To promote a digital economy, advanced technical capacity will need to be developed in some areas, but basic digital skills and awareness also need to be raised among the population at large to ensure that these technologies are used to their full potential.",""],[1,"46","1","Digital Skills and Literacy Investment","Investment in education and skills is vital to allow business owners and employees to make full use of digital technologies and innovate in ways that maximize its potential, while at the same time promoting the digital literacy of consumers.",""],[1,"46","3","Digital Awareness and Literacy Campaign","Raising digital awareness and literacy among the consumer base will be important to increase adoption rates for digital products, e-commerce applications and digital payments and remittances.",""],[1,"47","5","Digital Skills Development Programme","These skills should be developed through a combination of private and public sector efforts-in the school curriculum, through TVET and university offerings, and through lifelong learning.",""],[1,"47","5","Early ICT Awareness and Basic Digital Skills Education","For current and future users and consumers of digital products and services, education and training should aim at raising ICT awareness, starting from an early age to promote basic digital skills and the use of simple applications.",""],[1,"47","5","Advanced Digital Capability Training","More sophisticated training is required for those who will ultimately spur the development of digital capabilities and business uses in Samoa, including in the areas of programming, network management, and data analytics.",""],[1,"47","5","Tertiary and TVET Provider Capacity Support","Support should be provided to ensure that tertiary education and TVET providers have the capacity to deliver this training at a high standard.",""],[1,"47","5","Public Official Digital Skills Development","Digital skills development for public officials is also important to ensure that Government can lead by example in its adoption of digital solutions.",""],[1,"51","3","Education, Skills, and Digital Literacy Enhancement","Boost education, skills, and digital literacy within the population, to ensure that Samoa has the capacity to harness the full potential of the digital economy;",""]],"17":[[1,"46","1","Digital Economy Legal and Regulatory Reform","to strengthen the legal and regulatory environment to ensure that consumer interests are protected.",""],[1,"46","3","Digital Regulatory Modernization","Government also needs to increase trust in these products by modernizing regulations in areas such as cybersecurity, privacy, competition, and consumer protection.",""],[1,"47","3","Telecommunications Market Competition and Independent Regulation Reform","But to ensure that the benefits of these infrastructure developments are maximized, competitive telecommunication markets and the need for an independent regulator are key.",""],[1,"47","3","Tui-Samoa Cable Regulatory Strengthening and Regulator Empowerment","The regulatory framework for operating the Tui-Samoa cable system should be strengthened and the Office of the Regulator (OOTR) empowered to ensure that long term consumer interests are protected.",""],[1,"48","6","Digital Economy Regulatory Modernization","To increase trust in the use of digital solutions, laws and regulations governing electronic transactions, consumer protection, data privacy, and cybersecurity need to be modernized.",""],[1,"51","9","Digital Policy and Regulatory Framework Modernization","Modernize the policy and regulatory framework, and advocate as necessary to improve trust and reduce resistance among Samoans to digital technology and its applications.",""],[1,"64","5","Telecommunications Sector Competition and Regulation Reform","more can be done to promote a competitive, well-regulated telecommunications sector which would put further downward pressure on costs.",""],[1,"64","5","Reduction of Government Charges and Cost Recovery Fees","There may also be scope to reduce other government charges and cost recovery fees.",""]],"18":[[1,"10","2","Digital Business Environment Support Measures","A more supportive business environment - which can in part be achieved through the provision of complementary inputs such as digital payment systems, logistics and trade platforms - will also help to ensure that businesses small and large can take advantage of the opportunities that the digital economy offers.",""],[1,"46","1","Digital Payment, Logistics, and Trade Platform Support","a more supportive business environment - which can in part be achieved through the provision of complementary inputs such as digital payment systems, logistics and trade platforms - will also help to ensure that businesses small and large can take advantage of the opportunities that the digital economy offers.",""],[1,"48","2","Digital Payments, Logistics, and Trade Facilitation Systems","the government has an important role in facilitating the provision of complementary inputs including digital payments, logistics, and trade facilitation systems.",""],[1,"48","5","Electronic Single Window for Trade Compliance","The establishment of an electronic \"single window\" for submission of information to meet regulatory requirements, the increased acceptance of electronic documents, and the automation of customs processes could all help to reduce the costs of trade.",""],[1,"48","5","Customs Process Automation","The establishment of an electronic \"single window\" for submission of information to meet regulatory requirements, the increased acceptance of electronic documents, and the automation of customs processes could all help to reduce the costs of trade.",""],[1,"48","5","Street Naming and Addressing System Improvement","Physical (street naming) addressing systems also need to be improved to increase the speed and reliability of the \"last mile\" delivery of packages.",""],[1,"50","3","Digital Agricultural Information and Market Linkage Platforms","In agriculture and fishing, digital platforms can help farmers access information on weather, pricing, extension services and government support schemes.",""],[1,"50","3","Digital Payments and Financial Services Access for Farmers","They can also help farmers establish market linkages with potential buyers, and benefit from digital payments, access to credit and other financial services.",""],[1,"51","8","Business Environment Improvement Measures","Improve the business environment, including by taking steps to promote e-finance, logistics and trade solutions;",""],[1,"51","11","Global Outsourcing Services Industry Establishment","Projections of opportunity growth in business services are based on the assumption that a Global Outsourcing Services (GOS) industry is established in Samoa - moving in the direction of countries like Mauritius and Jamaica - which enables Samoans to participate in global value chains in areas such as business processing and back-office support.",""]],"19":[[1,"12","1","Non-Communicable Disease Control and Healthy Lifestyle Promotion","Continued efforts are needed to control non- communicable diseases, including through incentivizing improved nutrition, promoting healthy lifestyles, and returning to the family-oriented community engagement and fa'a-Samoa ways of delivering primary health care to the communities.",""],[1,"62","1","Human Capital Investment in Nutrition, Health, Education, and Skills","Investments in nutrition, health care, quality education, and skills development will allow Samoans to realize their potential as productive members of society.",""],[1,"63","8","Non-Communicable Disease Control and Healthy Lifestyle Promotion","Continued efforts are needed to control non-communicable diseases, including through incentivizing improved nutrition, promoting healthy lifestyles, and returning to the family-oriented community engagement and fa'a Samoa ways of delivering primary health care to the communities.",""]],"20":[[1,"12","1","Immunization and Epidemic Preparedness Strengthening","The measles outbreak and COVID-19 have thrown into stark relief the necessity of maintaining high immunization rates and strengthening preparedness, surveillance, and response protocols to deal with epidemics of communicable diseases.",""],[1,"63","8","Immunization and Epidemic Preparedness Strengthening","The measles outbreak and COVID-19 have thrown into stark relief the necessity of maintaining high immunization rates and strengthening preparedness, surveillance, and response protocols to deal with epidemics of communicable diseases.",""]],"21":[[1,"12","2","Climate- and Disaster-Resilient Infrastructure Investment","Government should continue to invest in climate- and disaster-resilient infrastructure projects",""],[1,"12","2","Robust Public Investment Appraisal and Debt Contracting Rules","Through robust project appraisal mechanisms and rules around the contracting of new debt, Samoa can take advantage of productive public investment opportunities while maintaining the sustainability of public finances.",""],[1,"20","6","Climate-Resilient Physical Infrastructure Investment","investment in climate-resilient physical infrastructure to improve connectivity and access to public services, and lower the costs of doing business; and",""],[1,"25","4","Climate-Resilient Infrastructure Investment","encourage investment in climate-resilient physical infrastructure to improve connectivity and lower costs;",""],[1,"64","6","Climate-Resilient Infrastructure Assets","More also needs to be done to ensure infrastructure assets are resilient to risks associated with climate change and natural",""],[1,"65","2","Climate- and Disaster-Resilient Infrastructure Investment","Government should continue to invest in climate- and disaster-resilient infrastructure projects",""],[1,"65","10","Public Investment Appraisal and Debt Contracting Rules","Samoa maintains robust project appraisal mechanisms and rules around the contracting of new debt.",""],[1,"65","10","Climate and Disaster Risk Screening for Investments","Given the critical importance of ensuring climate and disaster resilience of investments especially in infrastructure, community and landscape management, it is critical that all investments are screened for climate and disaster risk and that resilience building activities are integrated into project designs, and implemented with blended funding where appropriate.",""],[1,"65","10","Public Investment Coordination and Value-for-Money Procurement Procedures","More generally, the government needs to ensure that systems are working well to effectively identify, prioritize, coordinate and implement public investment projects, and adopt procedures that ensure value-for-money in procurement and design.",""]],"22":[[1,"12","6","Supportive Policy and Regulatory Environment for Private Sector Investment","Government policy will need to be supportive of long- term growth, and provide an attractive, stable economic environment to encourage private sector investment.",""],[1,"12","6","Foreign Direct Investment Promotion","This includes foreign direct investment, which has traditionally been relatively low in Samoa but which can be a critical source of capital, technology and knowledge transfer.",""],[1,"12","6","Public Goods and Business-Friendly Regulatory Support","The government should help provide the public goods and the policy and regulatory environment necessary for the private sector to flourish.",""]],"23":[[1,"11","4","Primary and Secondary Education Standards Improvement","Further work is also required to raise primary and secondary education standards, improve post-secondary training and skills development, and increase alignment with the demands of local and international employers.",""]],"24":[[1,"67","2","District Development Plans","the establishment of District Development Plans (DDP) to lift village level development is a step in the right direction and should be prioritized.",""]],"25":[[1,"65","3","Expansion of Reliable and Affordable Electricity Supply","Reliable and affordable electricity supply to households and industry will be expanded with a further increase in renewable energy generation and the extension of main grid throughout the country.",""],[1,"65","3","Renewable Energy Expansion and Grid Extension","Reliable and affordable electricity supply to households and industry will be expanded with a further increase in renewable energy generation and the extension of main grid throughout the country.",""],[1,"65","3","Solar, Dam, and Small Hydro Energy Development","Solar energy investment will increase further and the development of the Alaoa Multi-purpose Dam amd small hydro plants, while ensuring sustainable watershed management, will continue in pursuit of the goal to be 100 percent renewable.",""],[1,"65","3","Geothermal Energy Feasibility Assessment","Geothermal energy generation will be explored to determine its viability.",""]],"26":[[1,"65","4","Water Supply Quality and Reliability Improvement","Water quality and consistency of supply in the Afiamalu area and in the rural communities of Gataivai and Sataua in Savaii and Apolima island will be improved.",""]],"27":[[1,"65","6","Road Infrastructure Investment Programme","Investment in road infrastructure will continue, e.g. through the Second Phase of the West Coast Road.",""],[1,"65","6","Cross Island Road Construction Project","The Cross Island Road is expected to commence construction within the next few years.",""],[1,"65","6","Road Stabilization and Bridge Widening Works","The East Coast Road Stabilization, the Aleisa Road and the Lelata Bridge widening will be constructed within the",""],[1,"65","7","Road Network Capacity and Climate Resilience Upgrading","As the population expands into rural areas, the capacity of the road network and its climate resilience will be assessed and upgraded as needed.",""],[1,"65","8","Vaiusu Port Development Investment","There will be substantial investment in seaports with the development of the Vaiusu port, the viability of which has significantly improved given the congestion currently faced at the Apia port.",""],[1,"65","8","Asau Port Channel Widening","The Asau port channel will be widened and the Marine School port facilities will be upgraded to offer technical training at officer and higher levels.",""],[1,"65","8","Marine School Port Facilities Upgrade","The Asau port channel will be widened and the Marine School port facilities will be upgraded to offer technical training at officer and higher levels.",""]],"28":[[1,"36","3","Local Food Consumption Promotion","Promoting the consumption of locally produced food will also result in a healthier diet for more Samoans, strengthening resilience against non-communicable diseases.",""],[1,"65","9","Climate-Resilient Landscape Investment","there will also be further investments to promote a climate resilient landscape and advance priorities identified in the Community Integrated Management (CIM) plans.",""]],"29":[[1,"66","6","Strengthened Government-Village Council Partnership","This partnership should be strengthened.",""],[1,"66","6","Rejuvenated National Crime Prevention Strategy","Having a coordinated countrywide approach on domestic violence through a rejuvenated National Crime Prevention Strategy that brings together village councils, churches, government sector agencies, and service providers will have a positive effect in addressing social problems.",""],[1,"66","7","Community Policing and Judicial Capacity Strengthening","In some cases, increased police presence in the community will have a deterrent effect on trouble-makers, and help ensure a timely response to any request for assistance.",""]]}});